file tools/fixtures/f/fold_shelf_link_scan.sh the reading -- fold_depth_lost gated at zero, links_dead reported, code spans and placeholders read past
file tools/fixtures/f/fold_shelf_link_control.sh 47 behaviors over 17 pens, every refusal lifted in its own pen, the instrument proven blind-able
file tools/fixtures/f/fold_shelf_link_repoint.sh applies the one correction each link has, outside code spans, through the original inode
file tools/f/fold_shelf_link_witness.rish the witness, and the header carrying why four guards agree to look away
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri fold_shelf_link rostered tier lap, with the one-reason blindness written into its comment
file construction/REDS.md %486 booked and closed; %481 and %484 folded to their own shelf to make the room
file construction/archive/REDS-a-guard-that-cannot-hear-its-own-instrument-rows-484.md the shelf, header written by hand as the loom requires; written for %481 and %484, it carries %484 alone after a peer published its own %481 shelf mid-lap
file construction/ITINERARY.md the GRASS block carries the closure and the 890 named but not taken
recommend keep-going -- the guard is green on a control that plants each refusal and lifts it in its own pen, the repair is proven to have moved no prose by hashing four files with their link targets masked, and the class it closes fired a fourth time this morning while the lap was reading about it. One find is sized and unclaimed, and it belongs to whoever owns the fold rooms: the five two-level rooms hold at least 890 instances of this same class, measured rather than guessed, and the repointer that fixed these 345 needs only a deeper correction to reach them.
